var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/#Library-API","page":"Library API","text":"The exported names, and SshDataBridge.main, which is public but not exported.","title":"Library API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Configuration","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Actions","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Actions"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Results-and-errors","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Results and errors"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Command-line-driver","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Command-line driver"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.load_config","page":"Library API","text":"load_config(path::AbstractString)::BridgeConfig\n\nRead, parse, and validate the TOML configuration file at path. Every failure is reported as ArgumentError: a missing or unreadable file, a path that cannot be inspected, a file that grants any permission to group or others (it holds passwords; use mode 600), a TOML syntax error, and every validation failure. A syntax error is reported by its kind and line number only: the offending line may be a password line and is never printed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.load_config"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.parse_config","page":"Library API","text":"parse_config(dict::AbstractDict; config_dir::AbstractString=pwd())::BridgeConfig\n\nBuild a validated BridgeConfig from a parsed TOML dictionary. Every table is checked for unknown keys and every value for its expected type. [push].local_source_dir, [pull].local_destination_root, and the target keys name, host, user, password, and remote_dir are mandatory; every other key has a default. Relative local paths are resolved against config_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.parse_config"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.BridgeConfig","page":"Library API","text":"BridgeConfig\n\nComplete configuration: global transport options, push and pull parameters, and the non-empty list of targets. Target names must be unique, because each one names the local harvest directory of its target and two targets harvested concurrently into the same directory would overwrite each other's results. Two targets on the same host and port must not have overlapping remote directories, equal or one inside the other, because a project purge of one would remove the output of the other before it is harvested, and both would be deployed into one tree. The rule does not depend on purge_scope. Hosts are compared as node_key describes, IP addresses by value. The comparison concerns hosts, not storage: nodes that mount one filesystem, two names or addresses of one machine, and a symbolic link or bind mount on the node are not recognized. The rule is checked here only: the functions that take a single target act on the target they are given.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.BridgeConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.GlobalOptions","page":"Library API","text":"GlobalOptions\n\nTransport parameters shared by all targets.\n\nFields\n\nconnect_timeout::Int: SSH connection timeout in seconds.\nstrict_host_key_checking::String: default host key policy (\"accept-new\", \"yes\", \"no\").\ncompress::Bool: whether rsync compresses in flight (-z).\nbandwidth_limit::Int: bandwidth cap in KiB/s per transfer (rsync --bwlimit); 0 means unlimited.\nserver_alive_interval::Int: seconds of silence from the server after which ssh sends a keepalive request (ServerAliveInterval); 0 leaves keepalive to the ssh client configuration.\nserver_alive_count_max::Int: unanswered keepalive requests after which ssh drops the connection (ServerAliveCountMax).\n\nssh abandons a connection after server_alive_interval * (server_alive_count_max + 1) seconds without an answer from the server, 60 s with the defaults, so the transfer or remote command fails instead of blocking.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.GlobalOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.PushOptions","page":"Library API","text":"PushOptions\n\nParameters of the push action.\n\nFields\n\nlocal_source_dir::String: local project directory to deploy; mandatory in the configuration.\nexcludes::Vector{String}: rsync exclude patterns.\nrequire_clean_git::Bool: abort when the local git working tree has uncommitted changes.\nuse_gitignore::Bool: honor the .gitignore rules of the source tree during deployment.\nincludes::Vector{String}: rsync include patterns applied before the .gitignore filter, re-admitting paths the deployed project ignores; excludes take precedence. Empty by default.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.PushOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.PullOptions","page":"Library API","text":"PullOptions\n\nParameters of the pull action.\n\nFields\n\nlocal_destination_root::String: local root under which one directory per target is created; mandatory in the configuration. It also holds the rsync logs of every target, see transfer_log_path.\noutput_subdir::String: default output directory relative to each target's remote_dir.\nincludes::Vector{String}: rsync include patterns; empty means everything.\nexcludes::Vector{String}: rsync exclude patterns.\ncollision_strategy::Symbol: :resume, :backup, or :abort when the local directory exists.\nclean_remote_after_pull::Bool: purge the remote directory after a verified harvest.\npurge_scope::Symbol: directory removed by a purge: :project (the whole base directory, the default) or :output (the output directory only).\n\nclean_remote_after_pull cannot be combined with includes: a purge after a harvest narrowed by include patterns would destroy the files the filter left behind.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.PullOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.BridgeTarget","page":"Library API","text":"BridgeTarget\n\nA remote compute node and the layout of its campaign directory.\n\nFields\n\nname::String: unique label; it also names the local harvest directory.\nhost::String: DNS hostname, IPv4 address, or IPv6 literal.\nport::Int: SSH daemon port in 1:65535.\nuser::String: remote user name.\npassword::String: remote password; never printed by show.\nremote_dir::String: absolute base directory of the campaign on the remote host.\noutput_subdir::String: output directory relative to remote_dir (default \"output\").\nstrict_host_key_checking::Union{String, Nothing}: optional host key policy override.\n\nremote_dir and output_subdir are stored normalized: . segments, repeated slashes, and trailing slashes are removed on construction, so that every command names the directory in one spelling. An output_subdir that is . itself stays ., the base directory.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.BridgeTarget"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.probe_target","page":"Library API","text":"probe_target(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::ProbeResult\n\nCheck SSH reachability of target, the presence of rsync on the remote host, and the existence of the base and output directories. Connection, authentication, and spawn failures are reported through the result, never thrown.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.probe_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.probe_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"probe_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig)::Vector{ProbeResult}\n\nProbe every configured target concurrently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.probe_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.push_target","page":"Library API","text":"push_target(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::TransferResult\n\nDeploy the local source tree to one target. The log directory (local_destination_root) is created first, then remote_dir on the node, then rsync runs; the first step that fails ends the push with a failed result. On success the message gives the number of files and bytes transferred and the log path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.push_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"push_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nDeploy the local source tree to all configured targets concurrently. The source tree must exist, otherwise ArgumentError is thrown; when config.push.require_clean_git is set, it must also be a clean git working tree. Both checks run in dry-run mode as well.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.pull_target","page":"Library API","text":"pull_target(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false,\n            clean_remote::Bool=config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull)::TransferResult\n\nHarvest the output directory of one target into local_destination_root/<name>/. When clean_remote is set (by default it follows config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull), the directory selected by config.pull.purge_scope is purged afterwards, but only if verify_harvest finds the local copy complete. An incomplete harvest or a failed purge leaves the remote directory in place and fails the target, although the data were retrieved. With config.pull.includes set, a requested purge is refused with ArgumentError before any transfer, because files left behind by the filter would be destroyed. A local destination that cannot be prepared fails the target. Transferred files are appended to the log of transfer_log_path; the message gives the file count, the size, and the log path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.pull_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"pull_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false,\n                 clean_remote::Bool=config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nHarvest the remote output directories of all configured targets concurrently; clean_remote is checked against config.pull.includes before any target is contacted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.clean_remote_target","page":"Library API","text":"clean_remote_target(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions;\n                    scope::Symbol=:project, dry_run::Bool=false)::TransferResult\n\nRemove the directory selected by scope (see purge_path) on the remote host with the script of purge_script, run under sh -c; the default removes the whole project directory. The path is checked with validate_remote_path_safety before any command is issued; a refusal, by that check or by the script, is reported as a failed result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.clean_remote_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.clean_all_remote_targets","page":"Library API","text":"clean_all_remote_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nPurge the directory selected by config.pull.purge_scope on all configured targets concurrently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.clean_all_remote_targets"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.ProbeResult","page":"Library API","text":"ProbeResult\n\nOutcome of probe on one target.\n\nFields\n\ntarget::BridgeTarget: the probed target.\nsuccess::Bool: SSH reachable and rsync present on the remote host.\nssh_ok::Bool: the probe command exited with status zero.\nrsync_ok::Bool: rsync is installed on the remote host.\nremote_dir_exists::Bool: the base directory exists.\nremote_output_dir_exists::Bool: the output directory exists.\nmessage::String: diagnostics, as printed in the summary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ProbeResult"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.TransferResult","page":"Library API","text":"TransferResult\n\nOutcome of a push, pull, or clean action on one target.\n\nFields\n\ntarget::BridgeTarget: the affected target.\naction::Symbol: :push, :pull, or :clean.\nsuccess::Bool: whether the action completed with exit status zero.\nexit_code::Int: exit status of the underlying process, or -1 when no process produced one: the command could not be started, or the step was refused locally (unsafe purge path, unusable local directory, incomplete harvest).\nduration_seconds::Float64: wall-clock duration.\nmessage::String: outcome, as printed in the summary; never contains credentials.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.TransferResult"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.MissingBinaryError","page":"Library API","text":"MissingBinaryError(binaries::Vector{String})\n\nThrown when required system executables are not found in PATH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.MissingBinaryError"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.DirtyWorkingTreeError","page":"Library API","text":"DirtyWorkingTreeError(directory::String, entries::Vector{String})\n\nThrown when require_clean_git is enabled and the git working tree at directory has uncommitted changes; entries holds the git status --porcelain lines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.DirtyWorkingTreeError"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.main","page":"Library API","text":"main(args::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}=ARGS; io::IO=stdout, err::IO=stderr)::Int\n\nRun the command-line driver (probe, push, pull, clean; see usage) and return the exit status instead of calling exit: 0 when every target succeeded, 1 on a usage, configuration, or precondition error, 2 when at least one target failed. Summary tables, and the usage text when --help is given, go to io; error messages, the usage text after a usage error, and log records go to err. scripts/run.jl is a thin wrapper around this function.\n\nExample\n\nexit(main([\"probe\", \"--config\", \"config.toml\"]))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.main"},{"category":"section","location":"configuration/#Configuration","page":"Configuration","text":"One TOML file describes a campaign. It holds passwords in plain text, so load_config refuses a file that grants any permission to group or others. Create it from the template:\n\ninstall -m 600 config.example.toml config.toml\n\nUnknown keys and values of the wrong type are rejected before any node is contacted, and the message names the key. Relative local paths are resolved against the directory of the configuration file, and a leading ~ expands to the home directory. [push].local_source_dir, [pull].local_destination_root, and the target keys name, host, user, password, and remote_dir are mandatory; every other key has a default.\n\nremote_dir and output_subdir must not contain .. segments or the characters *, ?, [, ], which rsync would expand on the node. Two targets on the same host and port must not share a remote_dir or nest one inside the other, whatever the purge_scope: a project purge of one would remove the output of the other before it is harvested, and both would be deployed into one tree. Host names are compared without case, IP addresses by the value the C library reads, as ssh does. The comparison concerns hosts, not storage: for nodes that mount one filesystem, such as a shared /home on a cluster, configure one target for it or give each target its own remote_dir. A numeric host with a field in octal or hexadecimal notation (192.0.2.012, 0xc0.0.2.10) is refused, and so is one that the C library does not read as an address (192.168.1.256, 2001:db8:10).","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"configuration/#Template","page":"Configuration","text":"config.example.toml from the repository root lists every key with its constraints:\n\n# SshDataBridge configuration template. Install as config.toml with mode 600 and edit.\n\n[globals]\n# OpenSSH ConnectTimeout\nconnect_timeout = 10  # integer > 0; units: s\n\n# Host-key verification policy\nstrict_host_key_checking = \"accept-new\"  # one of: \"accept-new\" | \"yes\" | \"no\"\n\n# rsync compression (-z)\ncompress = true\n\n# rsync bandwidth limit per transfer\nbandwidth_limit = 0  # integer >= 0; units: KiB/s; 0 = unlimited\n\n# Server silence before ssh sends a keepalive request (ServerAliveInterval)\nserver_alive_interval = 15  # integer >= 0; units: s; 0 = ssh client configuration decides\n\n# Unanswered keepalive requests before ssh disconnects (ServerAliveCountMax)\nserver_alive_count_max = 3  # integer >= 1\n\n[push]\n# Local source directory deployed to every target (mandatory)\nlocal_source_dir = \"~/projects/sim_batch_01\"  # path relative to this config file or absolute; '~' expands\n\n# rsync exclude patterns for push (the default list)\nexcludes = [\n    \".git\",\n    \".github\",\n    \".vscode\",\n    \"*.swp\",\n    \"*~\",\n]\n\n# rsync include patterns applied before the .gitignore filter: deploy paths the project ignores\nincludes = []  # for example [\"/Manifest.toml\"] when every node runs the same Julia version\n\n# Apply the .gitignore rules of the source tree as rsync excludes (no '!' negations)\nuse_gitignore = true\n\n# Refuse to push from a working tree with uncommitted changes below local_source_dir\nrequire_clean_git = false\n\n[pull]\n# Local destination root: one subdirectory per target, plus the rsync logs (mandatory)\nlocal_destination_root = \"~/campaigns/sim_batch_01/harvest\"  # path relative to this config file or absolute; '~' expands\n\n# Output directory relative to remote_dir, for targets that do not set their own\noutput_subdir = \"output\"  # relative path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Harvest only files matching these patterns (empty = all files); excludes take precedence; not combinable with a purge\nincludes = []\n\n# rsync exclude patterns for pull (the default list)\nexcludes = [\n    \"*.tmp\",\n    \"*~\",\n]\n\n# Handling of an existing local directory of a target\ncollision_strategy = \"resume\"  # one of: \"resume\" | \"backup\" | \"abort\"\n\n# Purge the remote directory after a verified harvest (requires --yes on the CLI)\nclean_remote_after_pull = false\n\n# Remote directory removed by a purge\npurge_scope = \"project\"  # one of: \"project\" | \"output\"\n\n[[targets]]\n# Unique label (mandatory); names the local harvest directory and the rsync logs\nname = \"Cluster-Node-01\"  # starts with a letter or digit; letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'; at most 64 characters\n\n# Hostname, IPv4 address in decimal fields, or IPv6 literal without brackets\nhost = \"192.168.1.100\"\n\n# SSH daemon port\nport = 22  # integer in [1, 65535]\n\n# Remote user name\nuser = \"scientist\"  # letter or underscore, then letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'; at most 32 characters\n\n# Authentication password\npassword = \"example_password_1\"  # non-empty; no control characters\n\n# Base directory of the campaign on the node; no other target on the same host and port may use it or a directory inside it\nremote_dir = \"/home/scientist/campaigns/sim_batch_01\"  # absolute path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Remote output subdirectory relative to remote_dir (optional, defaults to [pull].output_subdir)\noutput_subdir = \"output\"  # relative path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Host-key policy override (optional)\nstrict_host_key_checking = \"accept-new\"  # one of: \"accept-new\" | \"yes\" | \"no\"\n\n[[targets]]\nname = \"Cluster-Node-02\"\nhost = \"192.168.1.101\"\nport = 2222\nuser = \"engineer\"\npassword = \"example_password_2\"\nremote_dir = \"/home/engineer/campaigns/sim_batch_01\"\noutput_subdir = \"results\"\n\n\n","title":"Template"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/#Internals","page":"Internals","text":"The functions and constants behind the API: validators, command builders, process runners, and the purge helpers. None of them is exported, and any of them may change in a release.","title":"Internals"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.CliOptions","page":"Internals","text":"CliOptions\n\nParsed command line of the driver.\n\nFields\n\naction::Symbol: :help, :probe, :push, :pull, or :clean.\nconfig_path::String: configuration file to load.\ndry_run::Bool: print the commands without executing them.\nclean_remote::Bool: purge the remote directory after a verified harvest.\nconfirmed::Bool: --yes was given, confirming remote deletion.\ntargets::Vector{String}: names of the targets to act on; empty means every configured target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.CliOptions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.assert_clean_git_tree-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"assert_clean_git_tree(dir::AbstractString)\n\nThrow MissingBinaryError when git is unavailable, ArgumentError when dir does not exist or is not inside a git working tree, and DirtyWorkingTreeError when the tree has uncommitted changes, including untracked files; only the tree below dir is examined. Returns nothing for a clean tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.assert_clean_git_tree"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_probe_script-Tuple{BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"build_probe_script(target::BridgeTarget)::String\n\nShell script executed on the remote host by probe_target. It reports whether rsync is installed and whether the base and output directories exist; every path is POSIX-quoted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_probe_script"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_pull_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_pull_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                   pull_opts::PullOptions, local_target_dir::AbstractString;\n                   log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing}=nothing)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the rsync invocation that retrieves the remote output directory of target into local_target_dir, with the filter rules of pull_filter_arguments. The password is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it. With log_file, rsync appends the list of transferred files to that file, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_pull_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_push_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PushOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"build_push_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                   push_opts::PushOptions;\n                   log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing}=nothing)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the rsync invocation that deploys the local source tree to target, with the filter rules of push_filter_arguments. The password is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it. With log_file, rsync appends the list of transferred files to that file, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_push_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_ssh_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_ssh_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                  remote_command::AbstractString)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the sshpass -d 0 ssh -n ... invocation that executes remote_command on target, with the options of ssh_options. The password is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it through standard input at execution time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_ssh_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_ssh_rsh_string-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"build_ssh_rsh_string(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::String\n\nConstruct the remote-shell string passed to rsync -e, with the options of ssh_options; the keepalive among them ends a stalled transfer with a non-zero exit status instead of blocking it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_ssh_rsh_string"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_verification_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_verification_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                           pull_opts::PullOptions,\n                           local_target_dir::AbstractString)::Cmd\n\nThe harvest of build_pull_command repeated as a dry run: --dry-run transfers nothing, --itemize-changes prints one line per item that still differs between the remote output directory and local_target_dir. Without --stats and --log-file, standard output is empty exactly when nothing the filter rules admit differs; files matching excludes are not compared.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_verification_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_local_binaries-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"check_local_binaries()\n\nVerify that ssh, sshpass, and rsync are available in PATH. Throws MissingBinaryError naming the missing binaries otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_local_binaries"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.command_string-Tuple{Cmd}","page":"Internals","text":"command_string(cmd::Cmd)::String\n\nRender the argument vector of cmd as a POSIX-shell-quoted string. The environment of cmd is not rendered, so the result is safe to print or log.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.command_string"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.config_file_present-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"config_file_present(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path names a regular file. A path that cannot be inspected, because a directory on it is not searchable or it ends in a loop of symbolic links, raises ArgumentError with the reason.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.config_file_present"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.default_config_path-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"default_config_path()::String\n\nconfig.toml next to Project.toml of the package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.default_config_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.drain-Tuple{Pipe}","page":"Internals","text":"drain(pipe::Pipe)::Task\n\nClose the write end of pipe that the parent holds and return a task that reads the pipe to end-of-file as a String. To be called once the child has been started.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.drain"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.ensure_remote_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"ensure_remote_directory(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                        remote_path::AbstractString)\n\nCreate remote_path on target with mkdir -p. Returns (; success, exitcode, stderr).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ensure_remote_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.execute-Tuple{IO, Symbol, BridgeConfig, Bool, Bool}","page":"Internals","text":"execute(io::IO, action::Symbol, config::BridgeConfig, dry_run::Bool,\n        clean_remote::Bool)::Bool\n\nRun action and print its summary table to io; returns whether every target succeeded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.execute"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.exit_status-Tuple{Base.Process}","page":"Internals","text":"exit_status(process::Base.Process)::Int\n\nExit status of a finished process: its exit code, or 128 + signal when a signal terminated it, which Julia otherwise reports as exit code 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.exit_status"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_bytes-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"format_bytes(n::Integer)::String\n\nRender a byte count with a binary prefix and one decimal: 512 B, 1.5 KiB, 5.1 MiB.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_bytes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_probe_table-Tuple{IO, Vector{ProbeResult}}","page":"Internals","text":"format_probe_table(io::IO, results::Vector{ProbeResult})\n\nPrint the probe results to io: one block per target, then a tally of the targets that are ready (reachable, with rsync installed). Fields that depend on a successful ssh command read unknown when it failed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_probe_table"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_transfer_table-Tuple{IO, Vector{TransferResult}, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"format_transfer_table(io::IO, results::Vector{TransferResult}, action::Symbol)\n\nPrint the outcome of a push, pull, or clean action to io: one line per target with its status, exit code, and duration, the message beneath it, then a tally.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_transfer_table"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_control_characters-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_control_characters(text::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether text contains an ASCII control character (0x00 to 0x1f, or 0x7f).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_control_characters"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_non_decimal_address_field-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_non_decimal_address_field(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host is a numeric address with a field in octal or hexadecimal notation (192.0.2.012, 0xc0.0.2.10), which the C library accepts and reads by another value than the decimal one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_non_decimal_address_field"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_parent_segment-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_parent_segment(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path contains a .. segment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_parent_segment"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_rsync_wildcards-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_rsync_wildcards(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path contains *, ?, [, or ]. rsync would expand them on the node, so that a transfer could act on another directory than the one named, while the purge removes the path as written.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_rsync_wildcards"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.is_numeric_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_numeric_host(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host can only be an IP address: it contains a :, or every label is a number, with or without a trailing dot. An all-numeric name is not a DNS name (RFC 3696, section 2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.is_numeric_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.is_valid_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_valid_host(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host is a syntactically valid DNS hostname, IPv4 address, or IPv6 literal (without square brackets, which ssh does not strip from user@host).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.is_valid_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.keepalive_options-Tuple{GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"keepalive_options(globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nssh options that drop a connection the server has stopped answering: -o ServerAliveInterval=<s> -o ServerAliveCountMax=<n>. Empty when server_alive_interval is 0, so that the ssh client configuration applies; an explicit ServerAliveInterval=0 on the command line would override it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.keepalive_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.map_targets-Union{Tuple{R}, Tuple{Any, AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}, Type{R}}} where R","page":"Internals","text":"map_targets(f, targets::AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}, ::Type{R})::Vector{R}\n\nApply f to every target on its own task and return the results in target order. Every task runs to completion before an exception of any of them propagates, so a failure on one target neither interrupts the others nor leaves a remote command unfinished.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.map_targets"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.node_key-Tuple{AbstractString, Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"node_key(host::AbstractString, port::Integer)::Tuple{String, Int}\n\nIdentity of an ssh endpoint when targets are compared: the host and the port. A host name is taken in lower case without a trailing dot. An IP address is taken by its value (see numeric_address), so that its spellings give one key: IPv6 groups written in full or compressed, in either letter case, an IPv4 address mapped into IPv6, a shortened IPv4 form. A name and its address, or two names of one machine, are not recognized as the same node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.node_key"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.numeric_address-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"numeric_address(host::AbstractString)::Union{Tuple{Int, UInt128}, Nothing}\n\nThe address of a numeric host as the C library reads it, and therefore as ssh connects to it: (6, value) for an IPv6 literal (inet_pton), (4, value) for an IPv4 address, shortened forms such as 192.0.522 included (inet_aton). An IPv4 address mapped into IPv6 (::ffff:a.b.c.d) is returned as that IPv4 address. nothing when host is not numeric or the C library does not read it as an address.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.numeric_address"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.parse_arguments-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_arguments(args; default_config=default_config_path())::CliOptions\n\nParse the command line of the driver. --help or -h anywhere, or an empty command line, selects the :help action. Actions and options match exactly. Throws ArgumentError for an unknown action, an unrecognized option, --config without a path or given twice, --clean-remote with an action other than pull, or --yes with an action other than pull or clean. --target NAME may be repeated and restricts the action to the named targets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.parse_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.paths_overlap-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"paths_overlap(a::AbstractString, b::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether two normalized absolute paths name the same directory or one lies below the other. The comparison is lexical and does not follow symbolic links.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.paths_overlap"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.prepare_local_pull_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget, PullOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"prepare_local_pull_directory(target::BridgeTarget, pull_opts::PullOptions)::String\n\nResolve and create the local destination directory of target according to the collision strategy: :resume keeps an existing directory, :backup renames it with a #n suffix before creating a fresh one, and :abort throws an ErrorException.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.prepare_local_pull_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.pull_endpoint_arguments-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"pull_endpoint_arguments(target, globals, pull_opts, local_target_dir)::Vector{String}\n\nRemote shell, filter rules, source, and destination of a harvest; shared by the transfer and by its verification pass so that both always compare the same file set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_endpoint_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.pull_filter_arguments-Tuple{PullOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"pull_filter_arguments(pull_opts::PullOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nrsync filter rules of a harvest. Exclude patterns come first and therefore take precedence. When include patterns are given, the harvest is narrowed to files matching one of them: every directory is entered (--include=*/), the include patterns follow, a final --exclude=* drops everything else, and --prune-empty-dirs omits directories left without files. Include rules alone would not narrow anything, because rsync transfers every file that no rule excludes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_filter_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.purge_path-Tuple{BridgeTarget, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"purge_path(target::BridgeTarget, scope::Symbol)::String\n\nRemote directory removed by a purge of target: the output directory for scope == :output, the whole project directory for scope == :project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.purge_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.purge_script-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"purge_script(path::AbstractString)::String\n\nOne-line POSIX shell script that removes path recursively on the node. It exits 0 when the path does not exist. It exits 98, deleting nothing, when the path is a symbolic link, whose removal would leave the deployed tree in place; when the path or the home directory of the account cannot be entered (a file, or a directory without search permission), so that their physical locations cannot be compared; and when the path is a directory that contains the home directory, which the lexical rules of validate_remote_path_safety cannot see. Each refusal states its reason on standard error. path is POSIX-quoted, without a trailing slash, so that the link test sees a link and not the directory behind it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.purge_script"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.push_filter_arguments-Tuple{PushOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"push_filter_arguments(push_opts::PushOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nrsync filter rules of a deployment, in precedence order: the exclude patterns, then the include patterns, then the dir-merge filter that applies the .gitignore of the source tree. rsync takes the first matching rule, so an exclude always wins and an include re-admits a path that .gitignore would drop (/Manifest.toml, for example).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_filter_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.reject_unknown_keys-Tuple{AbstractDict, Any, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"reject_unknown_keys(table::AbstractDict, allowed, context::AbstractString)\n\nThrow ArgumentError listing every key of table that is not in allowed, so that misspelled configuration keys fail before a run starts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.reject_unknown_keys"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.remote_output_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"remote_output_directory(target::BridgeTarget)::String\n\nAbsolute path of the output directory of target on the remote host, without a trailing slash. normpath keeps one when output_subdir ends in a . segment, and a purge of link/ would empty the directory behind a symbolic link that the purge script refuses.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.remote_output_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.remote_shell-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"remote_shell(script::AbstractString)::String\n\nWrap script as sh -c '<script>', so that it runs under a POSIX shell whatever the login shell of the remote account.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.remote_shell"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.required_value-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Type{T}, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"required_value(table::AbstractDict, key::AbstractString, ::Type{T}, context) where {T}\n\nReturn table[key] checked to be a T; throws ArgumentError if the key is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.required_value"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_local_path-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_local_path(path::AbstractString, config_dir::AbstractString)::String\n\nExpand a leading ~ and resolve a relative path against config_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_local_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_target_policy-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_target_policy(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::String\n\nReturn the effective host key policy of target, honoring its override when present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_target_policy"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.rsync_base_arguments-Tuple{GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"rsync_base_arguments(globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nLeading arguments shared by every rsync invocation: the sshpass prefix, the archive and resumption flags, -s (--secluded-args), and the optional compression and bandwidth settings. With -s the remote path reaches the remote rsync through the protocol and not through the remote shell, which would split or expand it under rsync older than 3.2.4 or with RSYNC_OLD_ARGS set. -v is not among them: a transfer records its file list in a log file instead, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.rsync_base_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.rsync_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"rsync_host(host::AbstractString)::String\n\nReturn host in the form accepted by rsync endpoints: IPv6 literals are wrapped in square brackets, everything else is returned unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.rsync_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_authenticated-Tuple{Cmd, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"run_authenticated(cmd::Cmd, password::AbstractString)\n\nRun cmd, whose first words must be sshpass -d 0, feeding password followed by a newline through standard input so that the secret never appears in any process environment or argument vector. Returns (; exitcode, stdout, stderr) and throws nothing: a non-zero exit status is reported, a signal-terminated child reports 128 + signal, and a command that cannot be started reports -1 with the reason in stderr. Base.IOError raised while writing the password is ignored, because it only means the child exited before reading it (for example a refused connection).\n\nBoth streams are read to end-of-file. Buffers handed to pipeline are not enough on Julia 1.10, where wait returns when the child exits, not when its output has been copied, so that the output could be read incomplete or empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_authenticated"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_captured-Tuple{Cmd}","page":"Internals","text":"run_captured(cmd::Cmd)\n\nRun a command that needs no credentials, capturing standard output and standard error, both read to end-of-file as in run_authenticated. Returns (; exitcode, stdout, stderr); a non-zero exit status is reported, not thrown, and a signal-terminated child reports 128 + signal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_captured"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_driver-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, IO, IO}","page":"Internals","text":"run_driver(args, io::IO, err::IO)::Int\n\nBody of main without the logger setup.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_driver"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.ssh_options-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"ssh_options(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nssh options shared by the direct commands and the rsync transport: port, host-key policy, connection timeout, keepalive (see keepalive_options), and authentication pinned to passwords. Public-key authentication is disabled and the preferred methods are keyboard-interactive and password, so that an agent holding many keys cannot exhaust the server's authentication attempts and an encrypted key cannot raise a passphrase prompt that sshpass does not answer; one password prompt is allowed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ssh_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.syntax_error_line-Tuple{Base.TOML.ParserError}","page":"Internals","text":"syntax_error_line(err::TOML.ParserError)::Int\n\nNumber of the line that showerror would print for err: the line that holds the position of the error in the source text. The line field of the parser is not used, because it is ahead by one whenever the last character read was a newline. It is the fallback, with 0, when the parser kept no source text.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.syntax_error_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_arguments-Tuple{Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_arguments(log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing})::Vector{String}\n\nArguments that distinguish a transfer from its verification pass: --stats, so that rsync prints its statistics block on standard output, and --log-file=<log_file> when a log file is given.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_log_path-Tuple{BridgeConfig, BridgeTarget, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_log_path(config::BridgeConfig, target::BridgeTarget, action::Symbol)::String\n\nLocal rsync log of action (:push or :pull) for target: <local_destination_root>/<name>.<action>.rsync.log. rsync appends to it, so the file accumulates every transfer of the campaign for that target: one timestamped line per transferred file and the statistics block of each run. Throws ArgumentError for any other action.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_log_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_statistics-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_statistics(stdout::AbstractString)\n\nParse the statistics block that rsync --stats prints: returns (; files, bytes), the number of regular files transferred and the total transferred file size in bytes, or nothing when either line is absent. Any thousands separator the locale inserts is ignored.\n\nExample\n\njulia> transfer_statistics(\"Number of regular files transferred: 1,234\\nTotal transferred file size: 5,368,709 bytes\\n\")\n(files = 1234, bytes = 5368709)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_statistics"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_summary-Tuple{AbstractString, Real, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_summary(verb::AbstractString, duration::Real, stdout::AbstractString,\n                 log_file::AbstractString)::String\n\nSuccess message of a transfer: \"<verb> successfully in <duration> s: <files> files, <size> transferred; log: <log_file>.\", or without the file count and size when transfer_statistics finds no statistics block in stdout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.typed_value-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Type{T}, Any, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"typed_value(table::AbstractDict, key::AbstractString, ::Type{T}, default, context) where {T}\n\nReturn table[key] if present, otherwise default, checking that the value is a T. A boolean is never accepted for a numeric T, although Bool <: Integer in Julia, so that port = true cannot silently become port 1. Throws ArgumentError naming context.key on a type mismatch.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.typed_value"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.usage-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"usage()::String\n\nThe command-line reference printed by --help and after a usage error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.usage"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_bridge_target_fields-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Integer, AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_bridge_target_fields(name, host, port, user, password, remote_dir,\n                              output_subdir, strict_host_key_checking)\n\nVerify every field of a remote target: name must be a valid directory name, host a hostname or IP literal, port within 1:65535, user a POSIX user name, password non-empty and free of control characters, remote_dir an absolute path, output_subdir a relative path, and strict_host_key_checking one of the accepted policies. Throws ArgumentError on the first violation; error messages never include the password.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_bridge_target_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_global_options-Tuple{Integer, AbstractString, Integer, Integer, Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_global_options(connect_timeout::Integer, strict_host_key_checking::AbstractString,\n                        bandwidth_limit::Integer, server_alive_interval::Integer,\n                        server_alive_count_max::Integer)\n\nVerify the global transport parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_global_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_patterns-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_patterns(patterns::AbstractVector, key::AbstractString)\n\nRequire every rsync include or exclude pattern to be a non-empty string without control characters, and one that rsync takes as a pattern: it reads a leading + or - as an include or exclude rule of its own, and a lone ! as the instruction to drop every earlier rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_patterns"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_pull_options-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Symbol, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_pull_options(local_destination_root::AbstractString,\n                      output_subdir::AbstractString, collision_strategy::Symbol,\n                      purge_scope::Symbol)\n\nVerify the harvesting parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_pull_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_push_options-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_push_options(local_source_dir::AbstractString)\n\nVerify the deployment parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_push_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_relative_subdirectory-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_relative_subdirectory(path::AbstractString, key::AbstractString,\n                               context::AbstractString)\n\nRequire a non-empty relative path without control characters, .. segments, or rsync wildcard characters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_relative_subdirectory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_remote_directory-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_remote_directory(path::AbstractString, key::AbstractString,\n                          context::AbstractString)\n\nRequire an absolute remote directory without control characters, .. segments, or rsync wildcard characters, other than the filesystem root in any spelling (/, //, /.). key and context name the offending parameter in the error message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_remote_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_remote_path_safety-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_remote_path_safety(path::AbstractString, user::AbstractString)\n\nVerify that path may be removed recursively on a remote host. The path must be absolute, free of control characters and .. segments, at least two components deep, and neither the filesystem root, /root, /home, the home directory of user, nor located under a protected system directory (/usr, /etc, /var, ...). Throws ArgumentError otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_remote_path_safety"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.verify_harvest-Tuple{BridgeTarget, BridgeConfig, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"verify_harvest(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig,\n               local_target_dir::AbstractString)\n\nRun the verification pass of build_verification_command and return (; complete, detail). The harvest counts as complete only when the pass exits with status zero and prints nothing; any output line is an item that changed on the remote since the transfer (a job still writing, for example). detail explains an incomplete harvest and is empty otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.verify_harvest"},{"category":"section","location":"#SshDataBridge.jl","page":"Home","text":"Deploys a simulation code base to several remote compute nodes with rsync over ssh and later harvests their results, on all nodes in parallel. One TOML file describes the nodes and the paths.\n\nThe README covers the command line: the actions probe, push, pull, and clean, their options, the rules of a purge, and the security model. These pages hold the reference: the configuration file and the library API.","title":"SshDataBridge.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Requirements","page":"Home","text":"Linux workstation with the OpenSSH client, sshpass, and rsync. Every remote node needs rsync as well, version 3.0 or newer on both sides. Julia 1.10 or later.","title":"Requirements"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"The package is not registered. Add it by URL:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/PaulGoG/SshDataBridge.jl\")\n\nTo use the command-line driver, clone the repository instead and run julia scripts/run.jl, as the README describes.","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Use-from-Julia","page":"Home","text":"Each action of the command line is a function that takes the loaded configuration and returns one result per target:\n\nusing SshDataBridge\n\nconfig = load_config(\"config.toml\")\n\nprobe_all_targets(config)                         # Vector{ProbeResult}\npush_all_targets(config; dry_run=true)            # Vector{TransferResult} holding the rsync commands\npull_all_targets(config)\nclean_all_remote_targets(config; dry_run=true)\n\nprobe_target, push_target, pull_target, and clean_remote_target act on a single target. SshDataBridge.main runs the command-line driver in process and returns its exit status:\n\nSshDataBridge.main([\"probe\", \"--config\", \"config.toml\"])\n\nThe library functions do not ask for confirmation. clean_remote_target purges when called, and pull_target purges after a verified harvest when clean_remote_after_pull is set. The --yes gate belongs to the command line. The rule against overlapping targets is checked when a BridgeConfig is built; the functions that take a single target act on the target they are given.","title":"Use from Julia"}]
}
